From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Strickroth <email@cs-ware.de>
Date: Sun, 3 Mar 2013 13:06:44 -0500
Subject: One process, many repositories

* Reset decoration cache
  This is needed for RevisionGraph to include new ref and excluded deleted ones.
  Related to issue #1663.

* Allow to reset and free refstore
* Allow to reset git environment
* Use a separate environment in libgit
* UTF-8 environment: be a little bit more defensive
  It is unlikely that we have an empty environment, ever, but *if* we do,
  when `environ_size - 1` is passed to `bsearchenv()` it is misinterpreted
  as a real large integer.
  To make the code truly defensive, refuse to do anything at all if the
  size is negative (which should not happen, of course).

* Allow to accept separate environment from TortoiseGit
* Allow to close open pack files
* Carry the TortoiseGit repository-switch hooks forward to 2.55

Signed-off-by: Johannes Schindelin <johannes.schindelin@gmx.de>
Signed-off-by: Sven Strickroth <email@cs-ware.de>

These three functions exist only for gitdll, which re-points a long-lived
process at a different repository. Upstream git sets up one repository and
exits, so 2.55 restructuring moved the ground under all of them at once.

odb_close_tgit(): odb_source became polymorphic and only the files backend
owns packs, so source->packfiles is gone. Downcast with
odb_source_files_downcast(), guarded on type == ODB_SOURCE_FILES because that
helper BUG()s on anything else and alternates need not be files-backed. What
this adds over upstream odb_close() is unchanged: closing the handles is not
enough, the store also has to forget which packs it found, because TGitCache
and gitdll outlive any single repack.

reset_setup(): the four file-scope caches it cleared no longer exist.
setup state lives in struct repository now, and is_inside_git_dir() and
is_inside_work_tree() recompute per call rather than memoising. The one that
did survive, git_work_tree_initialized, became repo->worktree_initialized and
is handled where it belongs, in repo_clear(). Kept as an empty marker rather
than deleted, because it names a requirement upstream has no reason to
preserve and setup.c may well cache again.

reset_git_env(): test the_repository->initialized rather than ->objects
before clearing. initialize_repository() sets the flag but not the object
database, which only appears later during setup_git_directory(), so a
git_init() that never opened an odb used to skip the clear and then trip
2.55 new "repository initialized already" BUG().

Signed-off-by: Refael Ackermann <refack@gmail.com>
